{"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Swidux","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"externalID":"Swidux","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"Swidux-logo","type":"image"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux is a Redux-style state-management library for SwiftUI. State lives in one observable store, mutations go through reducers, and side effects run as async effects. Macros generate the observability boilerplate. Built-in plugins handle persistence and undo\/redo. Optional plugins ship ready-made paywalls (RevenueCat or StoreKit-shaped), version killswitches, parental gates, analytics (Mixpanel or any backend), feature flags, and SwiftData\/iCloud persistence.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The dispatch cycle:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["View → store.send(.action)","  → willReduce hooks (UndoPlugin snapshots here)","  → reducer mutates state in place, optionally returns Effect","  → plugin reducers handle their own actions","  → afterReduce hooks (PersistencePlugin drains EntityStore changelogs here)","  → observer tree updates only changed properties (per-property observation)","  → effects run on a background actor; results dispatch back via @MainActor send"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your domain types and database stay in your app. Swidux provides the contracts, observability, and dispatch loop."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Companion-Packages","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Companion Packages"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Vendor-specific adapters live in their own repositories so a third-party SDK never enters the core dependency graph. Each ships a drop-in service conformer plus a preview mock, and publishes its own DocC reference:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/"},{"type":"text","text":" — RevenueCat adapter for the paywall plugin ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":", and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI"},{"type":"text","text":" sheet). See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Mixpanel adapter for the analytics plugin ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"text":"). See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Tutorials","anchor":"Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"]},{"title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/doc